<title>GERMANY: Schering, Gehe get EU approval for joint venture.</title>
<headline>Schering, Gehe get EU approval for joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Schering AG said on Tuesday that the European Commission had approved its plans with Gehe AG to acquire joint control of pharmaceuticals group Jenapharm GmbH.</p>
<p>Schering will hold 74.9 percent and Gehe 25.1 percent of the former east German group that manufactures gynecological products, Schering said in a statement. Schering said the deal is expected to be completed in the coming weeks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
